I've decided to snip a bunch more. There's pages and pages of blow by
blow detail. I want to summarize then talk a bit about my first ascension.

Summary
-------
Xanthian: with patience it's possible to get naked AC down towards -10. Staying
at XL 1 while cleaning out the upper dungeon of $ and gems with a leveled up 
pet can provide all the gold you need to feed the priest.

BAJ: Do it on the cheap down to naked AC 1 (maybe AC 0 if you still have money
to feed. Level up your pets in the process and clean out the Mine Town of
all decent goods and shopkeep cash. Then move on towards a regular game.


Xanthian Snippets
-----------------
But as long as I stay XL 1, I'm not in any need of being able to "contend"; 
the monster assortment is easily handled by my pets.  

I won't have any shame at all about starting the quest at
turn 100,000 even when not playing an extinctionist...

The only _requirement_ for high XL is that you must be XL 14 to get past your
quest master to the quest, other than that, high XL is almost entirely a
negative

There are lots of other ways to gain HPs,

I'm "fairly" happy with naked AC -4, which is usually
the best I can do, and will keep trying to do better
even than that as long as the money remains easy to
acquire; I'm not a diehard naked AC -10 targeter.

BAJ Approach and First Ascension Notes
--------------------------------
I just feel that XPs are tied to too many things (HP,power,slots,to hit and
damage bonuses,intrinsics) to negect for long.

So in my balanced approach I can accomplish 3 things in relatively short order:

1) Get protection.
2) Level up pets.
3) Gather cash for purchasing stuff

And pull all of this off in less than 3000 turns. But every turn that you
spend that isn't working towards getting you ascended, is a turn that is
adding to the entropy towards YASD.

Cleaning out the shops should be quite good enough to get to naked AC1 or
AC0.

I guess I'll use this post as my YAFAP. I'll use it to give some instructive
notes:

1) AC was critical in the early game. I found a bones with a +3 SDSM that got
me to negative AC. That along with an early spellbook of identify and holy
water, and GauntPow it gave my wizard the tools necessary to do the job.

2) Final AC was -30 with magic resistance, reflection, and unused "oLS.

3) Less than 65000 turns. And that's visiting absolutely everything in the
game.

4) Lucked up on the first altar I found. Had to go through Pestilence.

